  "model_card": {
    "summary": "A controlled addition base, concise/vivid fine-tunes and a conditional concise/vivid/JSON TinyLM with date-clarification templates.",
    "scope": "Separate generated content correctness from simple formatting rubrics and compare training-based versus prompt-conditioned style.",
    "limitations": [
      "Vivid style is one fixed metaphor template; these checkpoints do not establish personality, creativity or broad writing ability.",
      "JSON validity and content/style counts use a task-specific rule evaluator, not an independent general quality judge.",
      "Addition uses a finite 0–7 input grid and unordered-pair family holdout; held-out arithmetic is not arbitrary-range reasoning.",
      "Date clarification depends on explicit template fields indicating a missing date; it is not evidence of general uncertainty calibration.",
      "Held-out test arithmetic content correctness is 0 for the base, both default-style variants and each conditional arithmetic style. The conditional JSON branch is syntactically valid on 7/7 test items but has 0/7 correct sums; formatting success is not arithmetic success."
    ],
